#: includes/class-foliora-admin.php:3321
msgid "How do I resolve CORS (Cross-Origin) errors when loading remote PDFs?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-foliora-admin.php:3325
msgid "Browsers block scripts from reading PDFs hosted on other domains unless that remote server allows CORS. The easiest fix is uploading the PDF directly to your WordPress Media Library. If you must use a remote host, configure the header Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * on that remote server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-foliora-admin.php:3330
msgid "Why are PDF.js scripts excluded from cache plugins?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-foliora-admin.php:3334
msgid "PDF.js requires its worker script (pdf.worker.min.js) to load in an isolated worker thread. Combining, deferring, or minifying it with other theme JS breaks web worker loading. Foliora automatically sets data-no-optimize rules for WP Rocket, LiteSpeed Cache, Autoptimize, and W3 Total Cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-foliora-admin.php:3339
msgid "How do thumbnail generation and search indexing work?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-foliora-admin.php:3343
msgid "The first time an admin visits the Documents Library tab, the browser renders page 1 of each PDF and saves a high-quality cover thumbnail in your Media Library, while simultaneously extracting text so visitors can search for PDF contents using WordPress site search."
